{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the rain was upon the earth.</b> And further on it says ״וַיְהִי הַמַּבּוּל״? Rather, when He brought it down He brought it down in mercy — so that if they would repent, it would be rains of blessing; when they did not repent, it became a flood." "<b>Forty days, etc.</b> The first day is not counted in the reckoning, because its night is not with it — for it is written ״בַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה נִבְקְעוּ כָּל מַעְיְנֹת.״ So the forty full days end on the 28th of Kislev according to Rabbi Eliezer, the months being counted in their order, one full and one lacking — that gives 12 from Marcheshvan and 28 from Kislev."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:53.274504582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}